cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use knowledge, please cite it by its DOI, 10.5281/zenodo.23990335.
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'knowledge: Tests Fish Habitat Definitions Against What is Known About Where
  Fish Live, and Tunes Them from the Fish Records'
version: 0.4.38
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23990335
abstract: 'Gathers what is known about where fish live in British Columbia''s streams
  (life history and habitat values from the cited literature with their quotes, past
  reports, intrinsic-potential models, life-history timing and the provincial fish
  sampling records) and tunes from the records the gradient and stream-size thresholds
  of the fish habitat definitions the link habitat models use: it places sampling
  visits on link''s stream segments, scores candidate habitat definitions on held-out
  watershed groups, grades segments by expected use, and tabulates, maps and compares
  the tuned habitat definitions with link''s defaults. It also pulls PSCIS crossing
  layers and past-report tables for a group and checks stream names before a search.
  Under active development.'
